with one of the gang's leaders remarking on one of the gang's leaders remarking on one of the big sticks. one occasion that he wanted to hear zero comments about the Rosenberg job, because there were extremely powerful people involved in that particular hit. The C-Sig agents checked the gang's phone data for the time of Rodrigo's murder and were able to place many of them at the scene of the crime. Carlos Castro Sanna and his colleagues knew they had identified Rodrigo's killers. They just didn't know who had hired them. Or why? Sometimes the CSIG agents overheard the gang discussing impending crimes they were preparing to commit,

