at a gas station at 6.30. They were traveling in four different cars. By 6.40, they were at Rodrigo's building. The early morning streets were silent with no one to be seen. Waiting ready in place, the gang members just had to wait for the inside man to give them the signal to go. At 8am, the inside man called Medina, the intermediary, to give him a heads up that Rodrigo was about to go on a bike ride. The gang members were to follow him and carry out the hit then and there. Medina in turn notified William Santos Diva, who was parked by the apartment building in his black Mazda 6. Within five minutes, Rodrigo left the building on his bicycle and rode away. Santos followed him until Rodrigo turned onto a service road. Then Santos radioed

